# t09_binaural.ledc -- BOTH BINAURAL IDIOMS + beat glide + beat jitter.  ~55 s
# NOT therapeutic.  Feature family: binaural detune.
#
# TWO IDIOMS, and they are not equivalent:
#   (a) ONE channel with freqR set.  The generator drives the left carrier at
#       freq and the right at freqR and routes them straight to L and R --
#       "binaural bypass": when frequency_r > 0 AND != frequency, the PAN STAGE
#       IS SKIPPED ENTIRELY (audio_generator.c:1061-1063).  pan has no effect on
#       such a channel, which ledc_format.md does not say.
#   (b) TWO channels hard-panned -100 / +100 with slightly different carriers.
#       Both go through the normal equal-power pan, so each ear gets -0.0 dB of
#       its own carrier and nothing of the other's.
# Both are measured the same way: the FREQUENCY DIFFERENCE between the L and R
# spectral lines IS the beat.  Nothing in the recorded signal beats -- the beat
# happens in the listener -- so never look for a beat line in a mono sum.
#
# freqR CANNOT BE RAMPED.  ledc_format.md lists it as a prefix-capable compound
# cell; neither parser implements that.  atof(">250") is 0.0, which forces the
# channel to MONO and silently destroys the detune.  To glide a beat, ramp the
# LEFT carrier instead and leave freqR fixed, which is what B3 does -- freqR is
# the ABSOLUTE right carrier, so moving the left one moves the beat and KEEPS
# moving it (29 of 83 shipped sessions were silently not performing their
# central move until that was fixed).
#
# LED reference: steady 16 Hz -- a rate used nowhere else in this file, and an
# exact divisor of the 10 kHz ISR tick (625 ticks), so it adds no period error.
#
#
#
# CAPTURE-INTEGRITY CARRIER (audio ch15, 1900 Hz sine, hard LEFT, vol 40, from
# t=700 ms to the end of the file).  This is measurement scaffolding, not
# content.  A recorder can lose a block of frames mid-capture and still write a
# file of exactly the right length -- the missing TIME is simply absent -- and
# the frame-count check is blind to it.  Five such steps were found in one 665 s
# capture (~1 per 2.2 min), and one of them was written up as a firmware defect
# because BOTH optical sensors agreed on it: the whole recording had stepped.
#   python3 tools/avmeasure/captureintegrity.py rec.wav --carrier 1900 --audio-ch 1
# The tool needs a CONTINUOUS SINE: a session cycling square/saw/noise carriers
# gives ~369 us of phase noise against ~1 us for a sine, which inflates its
# self-calibrating threshold into a rubber stamp.  Hard LEFT so the RIGHT capture
# channel stays free of it for envelope and avsync work.  The marker window
# (0..600 ms) is not covered by this carrier; check it separately with
# --carrier 3000.
# CAPTURE-CHANNEL MAP used throughout sessions/test (see README.md):
#   capture ch1,ch2 = device headphone jack L,R   capture ch3 = photocell on
#   lane B's eye (LED3+LED4, mask 12)             capture ch4 = photocell on
#   lane A's eye (LED1+LED2, mask 3).
# --------------------------------------------------------------- sync marker
0     40 50 100 255 255 255 15
A 0   3000 0 70 0 1
600   0 50 0 0 0 0 15
A 600 0 0 0 0 1

# ---- capture-integrity carrier: continuous 1900 Hz sine, ch15, hard LEFT
A 700 1900 -100 40 0 15 0 0

# ---- ISR TICK PRIMER.  The flicker gptimer is DELETED whenever no channel is
#      left running and the next activation re-derives its tick from the 1000 Hz
#      FLOOR, so the marker's `freq 0` stop at 600 ms RESETS it -- the 40 Hz
#      marker does NOT pin the tick.  Worse, an update on an already-running
#      channel never calls s_ensure_timer_and_task, so whatever the FIRST
#      post-marker block sets is what every later block gets.
#      This row keeps ONE channel alive at 40 Hz for the whole file, pinning the
#      tick at clamp(40*250,1000,10000) = 10000 Hz = a 100 us grid everywhere
#      below.  mask 16 = LED5, which neither sensor can see (-78 / -74 dBFS, the
#      noise floor), and brightness is 0 regardless, so it cannot contaminate a
#      measurement on any unit.  It raises LEDC_MASK_HIGH_BITS (info) by design.
1000 40 50 0 0 0 0 16 0 0

# ---- LED reference, whole file
1000 16 50 100 255 255 255 15 0 0

# ---- B1  1..13 s : IDIOM (a), two channels, two different beats so the
#      spectrum cannot confuse them.
#      ch1  L 240.0  R 250.0  -> beat 10.000 Hz
#      ch2  L 400.0  R 406.0  -> beat  6.000 Hz
A 1000 240 0 60 0 1 250 0
A 1000 400 0 60 0 2 406 0

# ---- B2  13..25 s : IDIOM (b), two hard-panned pairs.
#      pair ch3/ch4  L 300.0  R 307.0 -> beat 7.000 Hz
#      pair ch5/ch6  L 500.0  R 504.0 -> beat 4.000 Hz
#      Expect the left capture channel to show lines at 300 and 500 only, the
#      right at 307 and 504 only, with >40 dB of channel separation.
A 13000 240 0 0 0 1 250 0              # silence idiom (a)
A 13000 400 0 0 0 2 406 0
A 13000 300 -100 60 0 3 0 0            # pair 1 left
A 13000 307  100 60 0 4 0 0            # pair 1 right
A 13000 500 -100 60 0 5 0 0            # pair 2 left
A 13000 504  100 60 0 6 0 0            # pair 2 right

# ---- B3  25..37 s : BEAT GLIDE.  Left carrier ramps 240 -> 243 linearly over
#      12 s with freqR pinned at 250, so the beat glides 10.000 -> 7.000 Hz at
#      0.250 Hz/s.  The ramp target is B4's ch1 freq (243), stated explicitly:
#      a `-` there would have ramped the carrier to ZERO instead of holding.
#      The literal 240 also MATCHES ch1's live carrier, because the firmware
#      discards the file's start value on a running channel and uses the live
#      one -- writing anything else here would make the file lie.
A 25000 300 -100 0 0 3 0 0             # silence idiom (b)
A 25000 307  100 0 0 4 0 0
A 25000 500 -100 0 0 5 0 0
A 25000 504  100 0 0 6 0 0
A 25000 >240 0 60 0 1 250 0

# ---- B4  37..53 s : BEAT JITTER, and the three things about it that are not
#      in ledc_format.md:
#        1. it is GLOBAL, not per-line -- one setter, no channel argument, so
#           ch2 below wanders too despite setting no jitter column;
#        2. it moves ONLY the binaural detune (current_freq_r = frequency_r +
#           jitter, gated on frequency_r > 0), NOT the isochronic mod rate, so
#           ch7's gate below must stay rock steady;
#        3. a period below 1000 ms is silently IGNORED (the previous period
#           stays), and the LED side additionally clamps amp to 5 Hz.
#      Amp is 1.0 Hz with a 5 s cycle (3.2 cycles in the block) -- deliberately
#      larger than the library-typical 0.3 so it is unmistakable.
A 37000 243 0 60 0 1 250 0 50 0 0 3 1.0:5000   # beat 7 Hz +/- 1.0 Hz
A 37000 400 0 60 0 2 406 0                     # no jitter column -- wanders anyway
A 37000 701 0 60 10 7 0 0 50 0 0               # mono + 10 Hz gate: must NOT wander

# ---- end: jitter explicitly back to 0 so it cannot leak into the next session
53000 0 50 0 0 0 0 15
53000 0 50 0 0 0 0 16                     # stop the tick primer too
A 53000 1900 -100 0 0 15 0 0            # stop the integrity carrier
A 53000 243 0 0 0 1 250 0 50 0 0 3 0
A 53000 400 0 0 0 2 406 0
A 53000 701 0 0 0 7 0 0 50 0 0
